  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Response in Malawi; El Nino, Cholera, ICSP _IMPACT 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam  and Catholic Development Commission (CADECOM) propose to support the response through various activities to improve access to safe water, hygiene practise, community engagement, case surveillance and promoting access to improved sanitation. Below are key objectives proposed for a 3 -month period to combat cholera in the targeted hotspot areas where Oxfam have already running programmes.  1. Increased knowledge and awareness amongst 10,000 people in high risk locations of Chikwawa and Nsanje districts. Mitigate against the loss of life and the spread of disease in four targeted districts  2. Improved access to safe and adequate water, sanitation facilities and hygiene promotion for women, men, boys and girls in affected communities  3. Increased case surveillance to mitigate the spread of Cholera in affected communities  4. Increased knowledge and awareness among 500,000 people (255,000 women, 245,000 men, boys and girls) on protection, safeguarding and safety in targeted communities</narrative>
  </description>
